From c1325ad53c5c930ab1a3bac52ac521a39ea731f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Chong <achong@meta.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Mar 2026 14:38:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 44/63] [cuttlefish] Fix AdbHandler shutdown on macOS to
 prevent thread leak
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Summary:
# Motivation:
Refreshing webrtc page will eventually freeze and fail to reconnect.

AdbHandler uses SharedFD::Event() for its shutdown signal. On macOS, Event() is emulated with a pipe and the returned SharedFD wraps the read end. The destructor called Write() on this fd, which silently fails because you can't write to the read end of a pipe.

This caused ReadLoop's Select() to never wake up, blocking the read_thread_.join() call forever. Each browser refresh leaked the AdbHandler read thread plus the cleanup thread waiting on join().

# Overview:
- use EventfdWrite() which looks up the pipe's write end from an internal map. This is backwards compatible — on Linux, EventfdWrite() calls the native eventfd_write() which works identically.
---
 host/frontend/webrtc/adb_handler.cpp | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/host/frontend/webrtc/adb_handler.cpp b/host/frontend/webrtc/adb_handler.cpp
index b26aba5a7..49eac7943 100644
--- a/host/frontend/webrtc/adb_handler.cpp
+++ b/host/frontend/webrtc/adb_handler.cpp
@@ -67,10 +67,11 @@ AdbHandler::AdbHandler(
 
 
 AdbHandler::~AdbHandler() {
-    // Send a message to the looper to shut down.
-    uint64_t v = 1;
-    shutdown_->Write(&v, sizeof(v));
-    // Shut down the socket as well.  Not srictly necessary.
+    // Signal the ReadLoop to exit. Must use EventfdWrite (not Write) because
+    // on macOS, Event() is emulated with a pipe and the SharedFD wraps the
+    // read end — Write() to the read end silently fails.
+    shutdown_->EventfdWrite(1);
+    // Shut down the socket as well.  Not strictly necessary.
     adb_socket_->Shutdown(SHUT_RDWR);
     read_thread_.join();
 }
